cross join (values
    ('Ornate storefront awning', 'Look for vintage fabric or metal canopies above shop windows with decorative trim, scalloped edges, or detailed brackets holding them up.', 'Detect a decorative fabric or metal canopy extending from the storefront with detailed ornamental design elements such as patterns, scrollwork, or elaborate trim along edges.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Canvas awnings from the 1800s-1900s were often treated with linseed oil and lead paint for durability, making restoration hazardous today.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/Porte_et_marquise_CCI_Nancy.jpg', 0),
    ('Faded vintage signage', 'Search for painted or printed signs on building walls that show age with peeling paint, faded colors, and weathered lettering from past decades.', 'Identify painted or printed text on storefront surface showing visible aging with color loss, discoloration, or deteriorated lettering characteristic of old vintage business signs.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Pre-1970s painted signs used fugitive dyes that fade in sunlight by design—cheaper than lightfast pigments and acceptable since signs were repainted every 5-10 years.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/Coppertone_sign_miami.jpg', 1),
    ('Art deco window frame', 'Find geometric patterns, bold metallic frames, and angular decorative elements around storefronts from the 1920s-30s era.', 'Locate window frames featuring geometric patterns, stepped designs, or chevron motifs typical of Art Deco style with chrome, aluminum, or decorative metalwork.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Art deco window frames often feature geometric proportions based on the golden ratio, reflecting the movement''s obsession with mathematical precision.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/Chrysler_Building_1_%284684845155%29.jpg', 2),
    ('Weathered brick facade', 'Look for old brick walls with visible mortar patterns, color variations, and natural weathering that shows years of exposure to the elements.', 'Detect brick wall surface showing visible aging effects including discoloration, mortar erosion, surface wear, and patina consistent with decades-old construction.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Historic soft-clay bricks absorb water and breathe, unlike modern hard-fired bricks; applying modern sealers traps moisture and accelerates deterioration.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Residential_neighborhood%2C_Lyons%2C_Nebraska.jpg', 3),
    ('Antique shop door', 'Hunt for aged wooden or heavy metal doors with original hardware, worn handles, carved details, or glass panels that serve as entrances.', 'Identify a wooden or metal entry door exhibiting age-related characteristics like worn finishes, vintage hardware, glass panels, or traditional craftsmanship from historical periods.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Solid wood storefront doors from the 1890s-1920s are often 2+ inches thick and made from old-growth timber no longer commercially available.', null, 4),
    ('Display window merchandise', 'Photograph items arranged in shop windows like vintage clothing, antiques, collectibles, or other goods displayed behind glass to catch customers'' eyes.', 'Capture products, goods, or items visible through storefront windows arranged for retail display showing goods from a shop interior.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Early 20th-century department store mannequins were anatomically incorrect (no knees or elbows) so displays stayed static between seasons—moving them was unnecessary.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Sv%C3%A6rtegade_3_-_shop_windows_02.jpg', 5),
    ('Historic street-level entrance', 'Capture storefronts at ground level with original doorways, steps, or thresholds that show how the building was designed for pedestrian access.', 'Show the ground-floor entry of a building with architectural features indicating age, positioned directly accessible from the street with traditional storefront elements.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Many downtown storefronts sit 3-5 feet below original street grade because cities paved over old streets rather than demolish buildings.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/Waterville%2C_Washington%2C_United_States.jpg', 6),
    ('Decorative tilework', 'Look for colorful or patterned ceramic tiles around doorways, thresholds, or lower walls that add artistic detail to the building exterior.', 'Record ornamental tiles on storefront surfaces featuring patterns, colors, glazing, or ceramic designs as wall decoration or floor accents.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Victorian storefront tiles were often hand-pressed and fired, making each tile slightly unique—mass-produced uniformity didn''t exist until the 1920s.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Iglesia_de_San_Ildefonso%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_01.JPG', 7),
    ('Original glass panes', 'Find old shop windows with authentic divided panes, uneven glass surfaces, or wavy distortions that show age and original craftsmanship.', 'Detect window glass showing authentic aged characteristics including slight waviness, visible imperfections, historical thick panes, or actual vintage glass material.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Antique window glass contains slight waviness and striations because it was hand-blown; perfectly flat glass is a modern invention and signals replacement.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Panoramic-windshield.JPG', 8),
    ('Vintage light fixtures', 'Search for old-style sconces, lanterns, or pendant lights mounted on the storefront that illuminate signs or entryways in traditional designs.', 'Identify exterior lighting elements such as old lanterns, sconces, neon signs, or period-appropriate fixtures mounted on the storefront structure.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Early electric storefronts used carbon-filament bulbs that were dimmer and warmer than incandescent, requiring different lens designs to project light effectively.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Oxford_Street_%28geograph_4949395%29.jpg', 9),
    ('Worn wooden storefront trim', 'Photograph carved or decorative wooden elements around doorways and windows showing wear, paint layers, or natural wood aging.', 'Locate visible wood trim framing the storefront with clear age marks including weathering, splintering, fading, or surface deterioration showing historical wear.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Historic wood trim often shows deep patina grooves from decades of hand-wiping and cleaning—smoothed surfaces suggest 20th-century machine planing, not original hand-finishing.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Morris_High_School_Historic_District%2C_Roughly_bounded_by_Boston_Rd.%2C_Jackson_and_Forrest_Aves.%2C_and_E._166th_and_Home_Sts.%2C_Morrisania%2C_Bronx_County%2C_New_York.JPG', 10),
    ('Period brass hardware', 'Focus on original door handles, locks, doorknobs, and metal fixtures made of brass or iron that show patina and authentic period craftsmanship.', 'Capture metal fixtures and fittings in brass or similar materials such as door handles, hinges, locks, or decorative elements showing aged patina.', 'rare'::public.item_rarity, 'Brass door hardware from before 1900 was cast individually, making perfect matches impossible; stamped, identical hardware indicates 20th-century replacement.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Hoyt_Public_Library_in_Saginaw.png', 11),
    ('Hand-painted wall advertisement', 'Look for old painted ads on building walls promoting vintage products or businesses with artistic lettering and faded colors from decades past.', 'Detect text, images, or designs painted directly on building surfaces as commercial signage or advertisements with visible brushwork and painted finishes.', 'rare'::public.item_rarity, 'Ghost signs (faded painted ads) can last 80+ years because exterior paint oxidation creates a protective layer that slows deterioration once the top coat fails.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Biles_Beans_sign_York_2012.jpg', 12),
    ('Iron storefront grille', 'Find decorative or protective metal bars, gates, or grilles covering windows and doors with ornamental ironwork patterns.', 'Show decorative or protective iron metalwork covering windows or doors featuring traditional patterns, bars, or ornamental ironwork typical of historic storefronts.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Wrought iron grilles installed in the 1800s-1900s were custom-forged by hand and cannot be duplicated exactly today without losing the original''s malleability and joint strength.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/Garage_door_sliding_up.jpg', 13),
    ('Arched doorway entrance', 'Capture curved or arched door openings above shop entrances, a classic architectural feature adding character to historic storefronts.', 'Identify an entry door set within an arched opening, curve, or vaulted entrance frame showing architectural style characteristic of older building design.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Victorian arched entries were often engineering solutions, not purely decorative—the arch disperses weight more efficiently than rectangular frames in unreinforced masonry buildings.', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Original_Store_-Bergdorf_Goodman_%2848064048193%29.jpg', 14)
